meta {
  name: List Hotdesk Sessions
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/hotdesk/sessions?personId={{personid}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  personId: {{personid}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~Authorization: Bearer {{CDRToken}}
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Lists active Hot Desking sessions for a given person — i.e. which workspace/device they're
  currently checked into, since hot-desk users don't "own" a device the way personal-line users do.

  **Parameters**
  - `personId` (query) — the person to check for an active hot-desk session. Bound to
    `{{personid}}`.

  **Usage**: Take the `workspaceId` from this response and feed it into "Get Devices For User" or
  "Find Hardware for WorkspaceID" to list the physical devices in that workspace.

  Reference: no exact public developer.webex.com page documenting this specific "list hotdesk
  sessions" REST call could be confirmed at the time of writing. Closest related documentation:
  https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/workspaces (see the `hotdeskingStatus` field) and
  https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/device-call-settings (Hoteling/device-member settings
  used to manage hot desking). Please verify the exact endpoint reference with Cisco/Webex support
  before publishing further.

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
